data.content:
Done. Here's the approach:

**`Clock.cs`** — an ambient context backed by `AsyncLocal<T>`, so parallel tests don't interfere with each other. Production cost is one null-check per call.

**Usage in tests:**

```csharp
var pastDate = new DateTimeOffset(2025, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);

using (Clock.Override(new DateTimeOffset(2025, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero)))
{
    var calc = new InvoiceCalculator();
    Assert.True(calc.IsOverdue(pastDate));
}
// Clock.UtcNow reverts to real time after Dispose
```

**Why this is the lightest option:**
- No DI container needed
- No constructor signature changes (callers unaffected)
- `AsyncLocal` is `async/await`-safe — each test gets its own scope
- Zero NuGet dependencies

For any other class reading `DateTimeOffset.UtcNow`, just replace it with `Clock.UtcNow`.
